VI(1)                     Funny CLI Manual                      VI(1)

NAME
    vi — Open a file in the built-in terminal text editor.

SYNOPSIS
    vi <file>

DESCRIPTION
    The 'vi' command opens a file using the built-in terminal text editor.
    It is an alias for the 'edit' command and provides a familiar command
    name for users accustomed to traditional Unix systems.

    It looks like vi, it sounds like vi, but thankfully it does not require
    you to remember 47 different keyboard commands.

ARGUMENTS
    file    The file to open in the terminal editor.
    Can be a relative or absolute path.

USAGE
    > vi file.txt
        Opens file.txt in the built-in terminal editor.

EXAMPLES
    > vi README.txt
        Opens README.txt for editing.

    > vi notes.txt
        Opens notes.txt in the terminal editor.

FUN FACTS
    - vi is an alias for edit.
    - vi and vim both use the same TerminalEditor.
    - No external vi installation is required.
    - If you type :q out of habit, the editor may judge you silently.

